    'male|a||The rehab programme: 82 500 of health, plus the 40 000 it saves — plus 122 500, and nothing was divided by anything.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'male|a||The drug: 247 500 of health against 400 000 of cost — minus 152 500.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||The threshold line is exactly the set of points whose net benefit is zero — so net benefit is the vertical distance from that line, read off in kroner.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'male|a||A quick check. A point sitting ABOVE the threshold line has:':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||Above the line the extra cost exceeds λ times the health gained, so NMB is negative.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'male|a||Now apply severity: for the most severe conditions the accepted λ rises to 825 000, and the whole line pivots.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||The drug's net benefit turns positive, plus 342 500 — and it now outranks the rehab programme's 287 500, so the ordering itself moved with λ.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||So what does net benefit still require of you?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'male|a||Net benefit removes the division, not the judgement: λ must be chosen up front, and the ranking depends on it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||Strip the picture away, and every option collapses into one signed number — Stinnett and Mullahy's 1998 fix for a statistics problem, since a ratio of two uncertain quantities has no well-behaved confidence interval and a difference does.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||Fix λ at the high-severity level, and each intervention gets a value in kroner.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||They rank straight down the column, and each is comparable with every other — not merely with placebo.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'male|a||Nusinersen: 1.8 QALYs for roughly nine million kroner per patient — minus 7.5 million, even at the most generous threshold Norway allows.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    male|a||And because these are kroner, they add up — across patients, across programmes, across a whole budget; ICERs never could.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    'male|a|grave|Net benefit doesn''t abolish the hard judgement, it moves it to the front: name the price of a QALY first, and the arithmetic stops fighting you.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
    '|a||Next: Where does the threshold come from - willingness to pay, or what we displace?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
